625, \"transitional_q2\": 0.1, \"permanent_q3\": 25, \"overload_q4\": 31.25, \"ratio_q3_q1\": 400}\n\nI'll use column keys: meter_size, accuracy_class, q1_minimum, q2_transitional, q3_permanent, q4_overload, ratio_q3_q1. Columns list must match keys. Use \"minimum_flow_rate_q1\"? Too long for repeated; use q1_minimum style. Let's define columns: [\"meter_size\", \"accuracy_class\", \"q1_minimum\", \"q2_transitional\", \"q3_permanent\", \"q4_overload\", \"ratio_q3_q1\"]; column_units: [null, null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null].\n\nTable 4 name: \"General characteristics of the family of instruments — Full bore, AC mains powered\".\n\nconfig_level attribute names: minimum_flow_rate_q1, transitional_flow_rate_q2, permanent_flow_rate_q3, overload_flow_rate_q4, ratio_q3_q1. axis strings: \"meter_size × accuracy_class — reduced bore, battery/renewable energy powered\" and \"... — full bore, AC mains powered\".\n\nNow write out everything. Let me be meticulous with numbers.\n\nReduced bore rows again from markdown:\nDN40 1&2: 0,0625 | 0,1 | 25 | 31,25 | 400 → 0.0625, 0.1, 25, 31.25, 400 ✓\nDN50 1&2: 0,1 | 0,16 | 40 | 50 | 400 → 0.1, 0.16, 40, 50, 400 ✓\nDN65 1: 0,39375 | 0,63 | 63 | 78,75 | 160 → 0.39375, 0.63, 63, 78.75, 160 ✓\nDN65 2: 0,1575 | 0,252 | 63 | 78,75 | 400 → 0.1575, 0.252, 63, 78.75, 400 ✓\nDN80 1: 0,625 | 1 | 100 | 125 | 160 ✓\nDN80 2: 0,25 | 0,4 | 100 | 125 | 400 ✓\nDN100 1: 1 | 1,6 | 160 | 200 | 160 ✓\nDN100 2: 0,4 | 0,64 | 160 | 200 | 400 ✓\nDN125 1: 1 | 1,6 | 160 | 200 | 160 ✓\nDN125 2: 0,4 | 0,64 | 160 | 200 | 400 ✓\nDN150 1&2: 1 | 1,6 | 400 | 500 | 400 ✓\nDN200 1&2: 1,575 | 2,52 | 630 | 787,5 | 400 → 1.575, 2.52, 630, 787.5, 400 ✓\nDN250 1: 6,25 | 10 | 1000 | 1250 | 160 ✓\nDN250 2: 2,5 | 4 | 1000 | 1250 | 400 ✓\nDN300 1: 10 | 16 | 1600 | 2000 | 160 ✓\nDN300 2: 4 | 6,4 | 1600 | 2000 | 400 → 4, 6.4 ✓\nDN350 1: 10 | 16 | 1600 | 2000 | 160 ✓\nDN350 2: 4 | 6,4 | 1600 | 2000 | 400 ✓\nDN400 1: 15,625 | 25 | 2500 | 3125 | 160 → 15.625, 25 ✓\nDN